clustine-terrain

Parts of this crate are adapted from SteelMC
(https://github.com/Steel-Foundation/SteelMC), branch `26.3` at commit
`885c4b3e60ed79862c37311780774f76806cb714`. Steel: A high-performance Minecraft
server implementation written in Rust. Copyright (C) 2026 Alve Jeansson and
contributors. Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or
(at your option) any later version; see `LICENSE` at the root of this
repository. The files that were adapted say so at their head.

src/noise_chunk.rs, src/aquifer.rs and src/fill.rs were written from the classes of
the pinned server jar, method by method, with SteelMC's
steel-worldgen/src/noise/noise_chunk.rs and steel-worldgen/src/noise/aquifer.rs read
beside them; each says so at its head.

tests/steelmc_hashes.rs holds hashes of the biomes of a few chunks, copied from
SteelMC's steel-core/test_assets/biome_hashes.json at the same commit, and reads the
whole of that file from a clone of SteelMC where one is named. tests/steelmc_terrain.rs
does the same with hashes of the blocks of chunks of the three dimensions from steel-core/test_assets/chunk_stage_hashes.json,
hashed as SteelMC's steel-core/src/worldgen/chunk_stage_hashes.rs hashes them. The
hashes are of values that SteelMC's extractor read out of the game.

src/surface.rs and src/biome/zoom.rs were written from the classes of the pinned
server jar and from nothing of SteelMC's. src/carver.rs was written from the bytecode
of the jar's carvers, with SteelMC's steel-core/src/worldgen/carver read beside it; it
says so at its head.

tests/fill.rs holds values that the classes of the pinned server jar computed
(tests/java/GameFill.java asks them without a server): hashes of densities, counts of
blocks, marked positions and columns of a few chunks. tests/surface.rs holds hashes
of the blocks of a few chunks that equal what those classes gave
(tests/java/GameSurface.java), and tests/carvers.rs hashes and counts of a few carved
chunks that those classes wrote (tests/java/GameCarvers.java). They are Mojang's data and not under the licence of
the code around them: see NOTICE.md at the root of the repository.

src/beard.rs was written from the bytecode of the jar's `Beardifier` and of
`Mth.fastInvSqrt`, with SteelMC's steel-worldgen/src/noise/beardifier.rs read beside
them; it says so at its head. tests/java/GameStructures.java asks the jar's own
classes for structure starts, references and bent terrain for the tests of
`clustine-structures`; it is Clustine's own, and what it writes is Mojang's data.
